<SearchLayout title="VVZ API - Privacy Policy" description="What VVZ API records, how the data stays limited, and your rights under the GDPR." keywords="vvzapi, privacy policy, data protection, gdpr, analytics, user agent" query="">

<main class="grow p-4 sm:p-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
        <header>
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="text-gray-600">
                VVZ API records as little as it can while running a fast search service.
                This page states what is stored, why it is stored, and what you can ask us
                to do about it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-1">
                Last updated 16 October 2026 · Applies to vvzapi.ch, its search interface
                and its API
            </p>
        </header>

        <section id="who-we-are" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#who-we-are"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    Who we are
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        VVZ API is an independently run, community-made search engine for the
                        ETH Zurich course catalogue
                        (<a href="https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis"
   target="_blank"
   class="link link-neutral">Vorlesungsverzeichnis</a>). It is <strong>not</strong> affiliated with ETH Zurich.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The controller for the processing described on this page is the
                        operator of VVZ API. Write to
                        <a href="mailto:contact@vvzapi.ch" class="link link-neutral">contact@vvzapi.ch</a>
                        for any question on this page, including requests for postal
                        correspondence details.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="what-we-record" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#what-we-record"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    What we record
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm mb-4">
                    <p>
                        Every request that is not a static asset or a metrics scrape is
                        recorded once. The record describes a request, not a person: there is
                        no account, no login, no cookie and no raw IP address in it. API calls
                        are recorded the same way as page views.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Search terms are recorded too: the text you type into the search box
                        or send as <code class="kbd kbd-sm">q</code> to the API, along with the individual filters of a
                        query. This is how we find searches that return nothing and fix them. A
                        search can therefore be personal without a name attached to it, and it
                        is handled that way.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                    <table class="table table-zebra w-full">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Field</th>
                                <th>Stored as</th>
                                <th>Why</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">client type</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">browser, crawler, app, unknown</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Tells people from bots, and sizes the service.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">client family</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">short label, e.g. python-requests</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows which tools and which crawlers use the service.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">user agent</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">first 100 characters, as sent</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">
                                    Recognises a client during an abuse investigation, and counts
                                    clients by family. Nothing else; see
                                    <a href="#api-users" class="link link-neutral">API users</a>.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">IP address</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">not stored; hourly-salted hash, 16 characters</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">
                                    Estimates visitor counts without keeping addresses, and
                                    cannot be reversed back into one.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">referrer</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">first 500 characters</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows which places send visitors here.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">url and path</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">first 1000 characters</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows which pages and API endpoints are actually used.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">query text</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">first 500 characters</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows which searches work and which return nothing.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">query filters</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">first 500 characters per value</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows which filters are actually used.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">result and timing numbers</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">counts and milliseconds</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">
                                    Performance work, and finding queries that fail without an
                                    error.
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">request metadata</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">method, status, page, limit, offset, order, view</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Diagnosing errors.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono font-bold">other query parameters</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-base-content/70">100 characters each, 300 in total</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">Shows which query options are in use.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="how-it-stays-limited" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#how-it-stays-limited"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    How the data stays limited
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        Records are pseudonymised when they are written rather than cleaned up
                        afterwards, and they expire on a fixed schedule. That comes down to
                        seven commitments:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
                        <li>
                            The IP hash salt rotates every hour, so a hash is a time window
                            rather than a person.
                        </li>
                        <li>Raw IP addresses never reach the statistics database.</li>
                        <li>
                            The user agent is truncated to 100 characters and serves two
                            purposes only: recognising a client during an abuse investigation,
                            and counting clients by family. It is never combined with other
                            records into a profile of you.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Search text is read in aggregate, to see which queries fail and
                            which filters get used, never to follow one person's searches.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Statistics are reviewed as counts per client type, client family,
                            query shape and result size.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Analytics run on our own infrastructure. The analytics instance and
                            the statistics database are ours, and no third-party analytics
                            provider receives anything.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            The statistics database deletes on a fixed schedule: 180 days at the
                            latest for anything you request or search, 90 days for the separate
                            search records (see
                            <a href="#retention" class="link link-neutral">how long records are kept</a>).
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        We do not sell data, we do not run advertising, and we do not profile
                        you for marketing.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cookies" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#cookies"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    Cookies and your browser
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        VVZ API sets no cookies and writes nothing to your browser's local or
                        session storage. There is no cookie banner because there is nothing to
                        consent to.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Searches travel in the URL. Your browser keeps them in its history, and
                        when you open a result we receive the page you came from as a referrer.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="network" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#network"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    The network in front of us
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        vvzapi.ch is served through Cloudflare, a content delivery and security
                        network. Cloudflare terminates the encrypted connection and hands the
                        request to us, so it sees each request in full before we do: your IP
                        address, the browser or tool you use, and the URL, search terms included.
                        It processes that as our processor, at the data centre closest to you, and
                        keeps its own logs under its own privacy policy.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Cloudflare is a US company, so a request to vvzapi.ch reaches a provider
                        outside Switzerland and the EEA. Those transfers rest on Cloudflare's
                        certification under the EU-U.S. and Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, and
                        on the standard contractual clauses in its data processing addendum.
                        Turning away floods and abuse before they reach us is part of securing the
                        service, the legitimate interest described under
                        <a href="#your-rights" class="link link-neutral">your rights</a>. For an
                        ordinary request Cloudflare sets no cookie of its own.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="reports" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#reports"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    Reporting a wrong course entry
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        Reporting an entry marks the cached copy of the matching source page for
                        review and notifies us of the entry ID. The report itself carries no
                        personal data.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="retention" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#retention"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    How long records are kept
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        The statistics database deletes records on a fixed schedule, by itself:
                        no manual step, and nobody having to remember anything.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Requests, i.e. page views and API calls: 180 days.</strong>
                            This is the record with the most in it (path, referrer, user agent,
                            the query text, hashed address), and it decides how long a search
                            term is kept.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Searches: 90 days.</strong> The separate search record
                            (terms, filters, result counts and timings) is deleted earlier than
                            the request it came from.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Deletion in the statistics database happens in the background while it
                        rewrites its data, so an expired record can outlive its lifetime by a
                        short while before it is dropped; nothing is kept past it deliberately.
                        A record also says less about anyone as it ages, because the address hash
                        salt rotates hourly and cannot link a record to a later one. To have a
                        record that relates to you deleted earlier, see
                        <a href="#your-rights" class="link link-neutral">your rights</a>.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        A second analytics instance runs alongside it, older than the statistics
                        database: Plausible, also on our own hardware. It records the same kind
                        of page views, but with no deletion schedule, because what it holds
                        identifies nobody. It sets no cookie, stores neither your address nor
                        your user agent, and its visitor identifier is a hash made with the day's
                        salt — a salt that is <strong>deleted after 24 hours</strong>, so the
                        identifier cannot follow you into the next day, let alone be traced back.
                        These records cover the page, the referrer, the browser and an
                        approximate location. They do not include what you searched for: search
                        terms and filters stay in the statistics database described above and
                        expire there on the schedule listed. Being unlinkable, the Plausible
                        records are kept as long-term history for trends instead of being dropped
                        on a schedule.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="your-rights" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#your-rights"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    Your rights
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        Request records are processed on the basis of legitimate interests
                        (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR): running and securing the service, keeping it
                        fast, and understanding how it is used. Where a request is answered for
                        you, processing serves the service you asked for (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Where the GDPR applies to you, you may request access to your personal
                        data, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing and
                        portability, and object to processing based on legitimate interests. No
                        automated decision-making with legal effect about you takes place
                        (Article 22 GDPR).
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Write to <a href="mailto:contact@vvzapi.ch"
    class="link link-neutral">contact@vvzapi.ch</a>. Because raw
                        addresses are not stored and the identifier we keep rotates hourly, we
                        may not be able to find records that relate to you; we will say so if
                        that is the case.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
                        supervisory authority: in Switzerland the Federal Data Protection and
                        Information Commissioner (FDPIC), or the authority in your own country.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="api-users" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#api-users"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    For API users: say who you are
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        API requests are recorded like page views, user agent included. A
                        library default such as <code class="kbd kbd-sm whitespace-nowrap">python-requests/2.32</code>,
                        <code class="kbd kbd-sm whitespace-nowrap">Go-http-client/1.1</code> or <code class="kbd kbd-sm whitespace-nowrap">curl/8.5</code> lands in the
                        same unnamed bucket as everything else, where a careless scraper looks
                        exactly like you.
                    </p>
                    <p>Please identify your tool using the usual convention:</p>
                    <div class="bg-base-200 text-base-content p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto">
                        <pre><code class="font-semibold">YourTool/1.2 (+https://example.com/your-tool)</code></pre>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        Your traffic then appears as its own family in our statistics, and if
                        anything about your usage ever needs a conversation, we can have it with
                        you rather than guess. Nothing is required, and anonymous clients are
                        not blocked. An identified client is simply one we can reach. The API
                        documentation is at <a href="/docs" class="link link-neutral">/docs</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="changes" class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h2 class="card-title text-xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-base-200 pb-2 group relative w-fit">
                    <a href="#changes"
                       class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute -left-6 inset-0 [&>svg]:h-5">
                        <icons.Link />
                    </a>
                    Changes to this policy
                </h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
                    <p>
                        When this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with
                        it. Questions, or a request about your data, go to
                        <a href="mailto:contact@vvzapi.ch" class="link link-neutral">contact@vvzapi.ch</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</main>

</SearchLayout>
